    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="1254" n="1242" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Hsu
                            Yung-chang to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 482</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-28">28 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inasmuch as Communist leader Lin Piao expressed his refusal to the 8 field teams
                    in the Northeast (including those for Harbin and Tsitsihar), it is requested
                    that you contact General Chou En-lai and talk with him for the speedy despatch
                    of Communist representatives of the field teams that they are supposed to
                        send.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d609-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hsu Yung-chang</hi></signed> (<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>)<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Govt.
                        Representative</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d609-f1" n="99" xml:id="d609-f1-content">
                <p>Notation at bottom of memorandum reads in part: “Mentioned verbally by Gen.
                    Marshall to Chou En-lai, who said team to Harbin had been sent and that their
                    disapproval of Tsitsihar based on fact Nat[ionalist]s refused to let 2 other
                    teams proceed.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
